# Cursor Project coordination

This file summarizes **Project-level** conventions for parallel Cursor Cloud
Agents. It does not replace repository policy.

**Canonical sources:** root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (workflow, branching,
quality, merge gates) and [`.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`](../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)
(linked from [`docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`](../../docs/CONTRIBUTING.md)).

## Parallelism

- Prefer at most **3–4** cloud worker agents in flight on one Project.
- **One agent → one pull request or one issue** (no shared PR unless the
  coordinator assigns a follow-up on the same branch).

## Hotspot mutex (one owner at a time)

Do not open overlapping PRs that edit the same hotspot without coordinator
approval:

- `Envy/Kademlia.cpp`
- `Visual Studio/Envy.vcxproj`
- `docs/DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md`
- `CHANGELOG.md`
- Root `AGENTS.md` and other privileged governance paths (see `AGENTS.md`
  rule 12)

## Git and PR hygiene (summary)

- Branch from `origin/develop`; names **`type/short-kebab-summary`** only
  (`feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `ci/`, …) — never tool/agent prefixes
  (`cursor/`, `claude/`, …).
- **Conventional Commits** on the branch; English PR title
  `type(scope): short description`.
- Format **changed lines** with `.clang-format` (do not bulk-reformat legacy
  files).
- Open PRs from the template (`.github/pull_request_template.md`); start as
  **Draft** unless the maintainer or coordinator says otherwise.
- Only the **maintainer** applies `stage:live-test`, marks Ready, and
  **squash-merges** onto `develop` (agents do not merge or bypass rulesets).

## Lifecycle

When a worker’s PR is merged or closed, **archive** that Cursor agent run so
parallel slots and store status stay accurate.